tools/pipeline/ledger.json:29771:     "note": "SECOND REVISION, on 7 of 9 seats (opus5 now landed; agy not fired).  THE FIRST REVISION, ONE ENTRY ABOVE, IS SUPERSEDED IN THREE PLACES AND SAYS SO HERE RATHER THAN BEING EDITED: it kept fbpending design-blocked on a cap derivation (the cap is the WRONG INSTRUMENT -- the bound is already gated by an equality); it kept four WDC files in one round (they are 3 + 1, and _sig's media blocker is MEASURED FALSE); and it counted six obligations (there are SEVEN, and my own deriver printed the seventh at check_probe_wiring.py:1328 and I read past it -- the third correlate-not-the-property error of the day, all mine).  Every Opus claim relied on here was re-verified in the tree before this was written: gate_offline.sh:1084/:1165, check_probe_wiring.py:1328, sig_probe.py:75, gate_asan_sweep.sh:99.  DISPOSITION, REV 2.  (1) TWO rounds, not one: `wdcaltoffleg' owns the three altoffset files (one module, one rig, one media family; the parent's `ok' first; _4bit's single-leg form is an ORACLE CHOICE and says so; _sig owes an oracle REDESIGN, not a bolted-on contract); `wdcsingleleg' is RETITLED to addtoinbuf alone, with the poisoned image and the endianness axis as its dependencies.  (2) THREE things are decidable TODAY and all three go in the wiringcliff commit after #516: hpcmips WIRED into gate_asan_sweep.sh BEFORE the :99 gate_skip, additive rows named, its EXEMPT entry DELETED in the same edit; fbpending WIRED with NO CAP as an apparatus-rot row named for what it tests, its EXEMPT entry deleted in the same edit, and the SM_EXEMPT fbpending_bound lane discharged the same way (it is the cheapest item in the set); the checker's FALSE comment at :1333-1334 and _sig's FALSE reason string corrected as L4s.  (3) The three altoffset entries re-dated naming `wdcaltoffleg'; addtoinbuf re-dated naming `wdcsingleleg'; each DELETED in the same edit as its wiring when its round ships.  (4) NEW ROW `witnessclassdoor' (med): the CLASS_WITNESS field is an undated door for un-gated detectors; the fix is a class rule with a dated cutoff, like every checker change here -- its own round, not a rider.  On the record: the ledger's EIGHT was an expired measurement (8 -> 7 -> 6), not a transcription; DERIVED section 9 corrects section 1."
tools/pipeline/ledger.json:29789:     "ev": "regress/artifacts/wiringcliff/codex_fbpending_20260910.err",
tools/pipeline/ledger.json:29791:     "note": "GPT-6 Astra @ max, file-reading (brief_fbpending_20260910.md); no refusal; read-only python checks of the checker's scanner against shell text in memory.  CORRECTS THREE PREMISES OF THE BRIEF: (1) the dated EXEMPT entry is on `fbpending_drain_probe.py' (REPORT-ONLY, EXPECT_CAP), NOT on fbpending_witness.py -- wiring the witness does not discharge it, keep it; (2) no candidate gate literally satisfies `free-runs guests with no wall-clock oracle': gate_hygiene runs no guest, gate_offline runs differentials, gate_ab runs long guests but keeps its stall/backstop oracles -- host it in gate_ab.sh SERIALIZED AFTER all existing A/B work, and convert gate_ab.sh:66's `need_exec' (which exits via gate_skip and would make the appended witness vanish whenever a baseline binary is missing) into a conditional with a `degrade' else-arm; (3) the witness becomes CLASS_DETECTOR once gated (`#442 post-fix apparatus: controls, coverage, no clock freeze'), or the checker reports GATED WITNESS.  Supplied the full section text: the gate creates the four-byte little-endian ARM NOP stub itself (neither the gate nor the witness has a fixture), runs `python3 \"$HERE/fbpending_witness.py\" \"$ROOT/build/gxemul\" \"$FBPENDING_STUB\"', and checks exit status, >= 12 control rows, CONTROL=OK, COVERAGE=OK (prefix match -- the line carries an explanatory suffix), SYMPTOM=ABSENT and VERDICT=PASS as separate rows so `not run long enough' and `broken' cannot render alike; ~2 min budget, source-derived.  The selfmutant lane: a `selfmutant_one' line for diff_fbpending_bound with FBBOUND_PASS/FAIL as the verdict contract, plus replacing gate_offline.sh:1263's missing-object `note' with a `degrade' (otherwise the section can omit the value gate while merely printing a note); the helper runs its binary without arguments so R2 stays skipped while R3/R4 exercise the mutant; `exempt_expired' is strict `<', so a 09-20 exemption first reds on 09-21 (as DERIVED_20260909 said).  Verified the checker derives gate scripts from run.sh's GATES array, recognises a python interpreter at command position with `$HERE' paths, excludes comments and heredocs, and would find the quoted invocation.  Could not verify the NO-CAP ruling itself (took it from the packet).  These edits are the wiringcliff commit's fbpending half."
