tools/pipeline/ledger.json:51311:   "state_note": "FILED 2026-09-17 by the #531 pass-2 opus5 seat as the nearest SIBLING of ip30abortkill.  Two structurally identical `fatal(\"TODO: ip22 legacy interrupt rewrite!\"); abort();' pairs in dev_sgi_ip22.c, in the WRITE arms of the local0 and local1 interrupt masks.  *** THE CENSUS LESSON RECURS: these carry no `exit(', so the same three exit( sweeps that walked past #531's four sites walk past these too.  A census keyed on `exit(' cannot see a host death spelled abort(). ***  Ranked HIGH on the same warrant as #531: guest-reachable host death on an advertised machine. The disposition is likely the same as #531's -- heart.h has no ip22 equivalent, so the option-set work starts from the file's own sibling handlers.  LINE NUMBERS VERIFIED 2026-09-17 by opening the file: :314 and :338 exactly, 2 abort() and 0 exit( in dev_sgi_ip22.c.  Grade upgraded BELIEVED -> CONFIRMED.  *** SEVERITY CORRECTED HIGH -> LOW THE SAME DAY IT WAS FILED, AND THE CORRECTION IS MINE TO OWN: I RANKED IT AS A SIBLING OF #531 WITHOUT CHECKING THE ONE FACT THAT MADE #531 LIVE. ***  #531's warrant is that `-E sgi -e ip30' is an ADVERTISED machine AND the device is actually installed -- its rung-3 probe reached the code and killed the host, empirically.  dev_sgi_ip22 is DIFFERENT and the difference is decisive:  (a) `dev_sgi_ip22_init' has exactly TWO call sites in the whole tree, machine_sgi.c:270 and :278, and BOTH ARE COMMENTED OUT;  (b) the file defines DEVICE_ACCESS(sgi_ip22) but NO DEVINIT(sgi_ip22), so the autodev / device_add route cannot register it either;  (c) it still COMPILES IN (Makefile.skel lists dev_sgi_ip22.o), which is why an abort()-census finds it and a reachability question does not get asked.  *** THE DEVICE IS NEVER IN ANY MACHINE'S MEMORY MAP, SO NO GUEST CAN REACH EITHER abort(). ***  CONSEQUENCE FOR THE WITNESS LADDER, and it is why this cannot simply be 'done later': NO WITNESS EXISTS OR CAN EXIST AT RUNGS 2-4 while the device is uninstalled, and installing it to reach the site is exactly what the ladder names as LAUNDERING -- 'a machine or device_add introduced IN ORDER TO reach the site is laundering, not witnessing'.  So this is DOCUMENTED-ONLY unless and until something installs the device for its own reasons.  IT REMAINS WORTH KEEPING rather than dropping: the sites are dead code carrying a host kill, and the day anyone re-enables those two commented lines they become live immediately, with no review in between.  *** THE CENSUS LESSON STANDS UNCHANGED AND IS THE REAL VALUE HERE: 2 abort() and 0 exit( in this file, so the same three exit( sweeps that walked past #531's four sites walk past these two. ***  A census keyed on `exit(' cannot see a host death spelled abort() -- whether or not the code is reachable.",
tools/pipeline/ledger.json:51341:   "state_note": "*** THE FOURTH RECORDED INSTANCE OF THE UNREAD-REVIEW CLASS, AND THE MOST PRECISE: THE MISSING ROW WAS PRESCRIBED BY NAME, IN ONE LINE, IN A DURABLE ARTIFACT, BEFORE THE FIX SHIPPED. ***  regress/artifacts/ip30abortkill/FIXDIFF_grok_20260917.txt:239 reads: '5. `isr 20 rd' / `isr 28 rd' -- load does not clobber ISR; load's VALUE is not the seeded ISR (don't-mirror)'.  BOTH rows, explicitly.  The round shipped `isr 20 rd val' and not its sibling, and it then cost a full extra kill table and a nine-seat adjudication pass to rediscover -- with agy REQUIRING it and grok having to point at its own earlier answer.  The opus5 seat independently reported the same pattern: grok's design pass prescribed six closing rows and items 1, 2, 4 and 5 did not ship.  *** THE STRUCTURAL GAP, WHICH IS THE PART WORTH KEEPING: THE CARRIER'S EXISTING RULE CANNOT CATCH THIS. ***  After #490 the rule is 'a row list rewritten from a panel's findings is DIFFED against the pre-table block's own prescribed rows, not merely extended with the new ones.'  That binds the PRETABLE.  Here the prescription NEVER ENTERED A PRETABLE -- it lived in a SEAT'S FIX-DESIGN ANSWER, and nothing diffs a row list against that.  So the #490 rule was obeyed and the row was still lost: the diff ran against the wrong source document.  AND THE PRETABLE MADE IT WORSE RATHER THAN NEUTRAL: PRETABLE.out listed BOTH read arms as 'decline, no value to pin', so the one artifact #490 DOES mandate diffing against positively asserted that neither row was owed.  *A pre-table block that mis-classifies a cell does not merely fail to catch the omission; it CERTIFIES it.*  grok's correction is one sentence: A DECLINE HAS A VALUE, AND IT IS 0.  PROPOSED REMEDY, FILED NOT BUILT (a harness change owing two negative controls): a round whose fix design was reviewed by a seat DIFFS ITS FINAL ROW LIST AGAINST THAT SEAT'S PRESCRIBED ROWS, as #490 mandates for the PRETABLE -- and the PRETABLE should CARRY those prescriptions forward so the two documents cannot disagree silently.  Cheapest mechanical form is existence-only: if a FIXDIFF_<seat>_*.txt sits beside the killtable dir, each of its numbered prescriptions must map to a shipped row or an explicit no-row sentence.  *** THE LAST FIVE UNREAD ANSWERS READ 2026-09-18 (panel_20260827_134019).  23 OF 23 NOW READ -- the section-G backlog is CLEARED. ***  This was a pass-1 DESIGN panel on a now-CLOSED row, so it was read for the question `seatprescriptiondiff' exists to ask: DID THE PRESCRIPTIONS SURVIVE INTO THE SHIPPED WORK?  *** AND THE ANSWER IS YES -- A NEGATIVE RESULT THAT BOUNDS THE ROW I FILED THIS MORNING. ***  agy prescribed three items.  (1) the predicate fix -- SHIPPED, dev_wdc.c now triggers on WDCTL_RST (0x04) and not WDCTL_4BIT (0x08), with the rising-edge `prev_ctl' machinery and a recorded brace hazard beside it.  (2) the MACHINE_LANDISK alt-status mapping -- NOT in dev_wdc.c, and NOT a silent drop: it was SPLIT INTO ITS OWN ROW `landiskaux', which is open, and OUTSTANDING_BUGS carries the coupling in full.  (3) acceptance rows -- folded, per the kimi/deepseek rulings in the same panel.  *** SO `seatprescriptiondiff' HAS A POPULATION OF ONE (the #531 case), NOT A PATTERN.  A class filed from a single instance is a hypothesis, and this is the first test of it -- it did not generalise.  Recorded as such rather than left looking systemic. ***  AND THE COUPLING WAS HANDLED IN THE SAFE ORDER, which is worth keeping because the unsafe one was live: mapping the landisk register WHILE the predicate still triggered on 0x08 would have latched COMMAND_RESET on SIX routine Device Control writes per probe (a seat measured twelve writes, six of them 0x08, currently all landing on unmapped memory).  The round fixed the PREDICATE first, so `wdcaltctrlbit' is CLOSED as overtaken and `landiskaux' is now OPEN AND UNBLOCKED.  *** THAT MAKES `landiskaux' A ONE-LINE FIX THAT IS NOW SAFE TO TAKE -- a strong critical-and-easily-resolvable candidate for the next round. ***  The other seats' content was design judgement, no live defects: glm listed SEVEN uninlined premises and ranked them by load-bearingness (the premise-audit discipline working as intended); minimax named an option-set hole (C4/B5, 'the brief's C-options jump'); deepseek ruled that a channel reset must clear in-flight transfer, FIFO, phase and interrupt state but NOT per-device-life diagnostics like `warned_*' -- and dev_wdc.c carries 43 `warned_' references, so that distinction is load-bearing there.",
tools/pipeline/ledger.json:51349:     "ev": "regress/artifacts/ip30abortkill/FIXDIFF_grok_20260917.txt:239",
tools/pipeline/ledger.json:63364:   "state_note": "[2026-10-18, #565] THE rldicl HALF IS DISCHARGED, MEASURED with the medium this row names: an IDENTITY BODY for X(rldicl) -- decode and retire, write nothing -- built in a scratch clone of build/ scores SCORE 16/24 and reds 11 of gate 13's 30 rldicl checks; restored, 24/24, clone cmp-clean and the binary fresh (regress/artifacts/ppcrldiclzero/gatewire_20261018/nullmedium/identity/IDENTITY.out).  Also measured: /bin/true 22 of 30; an absent binary reds the sentinel in the block's scoring text and is a SKIP in gate 13 (need_exec).  The probe is now wired with equality pins, so the by-construction reading holds as well.  The alpha_tbi_probe.py half is STILL OWED (its exemption comes due 2026-10-22).  ||  filed 2026-10-09 from Fable 5.1's 7n-1 ruling (regress/artifacts/fablequeue7n_20261009/fable5_rule7n_12.md: a by-construction claim is checked by READING the gate's pin form, and a table failing that reading owes a measured leg) as corrected by GPT-6 Astra (regress/artifacts/fablequeue7n_20261009/codex_astra_confirm.txt item 1: both probes lack runtime wiring and fixed denominator checks; their exemptions sit in tools/pipeline/check_probe_wiring.py).  The ruling had predicted this population at ZERO.  The leg's object, per the carrier's clause-(c) block: an instruction handler's IDENTITY BODY (decode and retire, write nothing) -- two measured instances at #527.  Their tables' 'null medium' labels were whole-file PRE-FIX legs (clause (a)); those labels are corrected in the same commit that filed this row.  ppc_rldicl_probe.py's own gate wiring is separately exempt until 2026-10-22 (04f3e7c0)."
tools/pipeline/ledger.json:64138:   "state_note": "filed 2026-10-18 by #565 (the gate wiring of this probe).  Raised by GPT-6 Astra, Grok 4.7 and GLM 5.3 on #565's pass 2: all three seats ruled the WITNESS label and the usage string FILE, not fix (GPT-6 Astra adding the runtime banner); the split note is Grok 4.7's F2 finding, filed by the author with no seat's ruling on it.  Section R reports the first as an ADVISORY `SELFLABEL' note (check_probe_wiring.py's self_label; it fails nothing); the usage string prints only when the probe gets fewer than two arguments, which gate 13 never does; the split note is Grok 4.7's (#565 F2).  Cosmetic: no gate, kill or score rests on any of the three.  A round touching the probe's docstring -- `ppcprobescorestale''s demotion is the next one -- can close it."
tools/pipeline/ledger.json:64147:   "title": "#527's five residuals, moved here from `ppcrldimimask` at its closure: the SH=63/MB=1 full-mask rldimi row, the wrapping stale-rS alias row, the Rc=1-only insertion skip, CENSUS_SHRINK and R_NOGUARD -- coverage debt and named measurements on regress/ppc_rlwimi_probe.py and ppc_rldimi_probe.py, none a floor breach",
tools/pipeline/ledger.json:64148:   "state_note": "filed 2026-10-18 by #527's closure-records commit.  Fable 5.1's 2026-09-12 closing ruling (regress/artifacts/xscaleinten/fable_adjudication_20260912.md) graded each clause (e) or a named measurement, not owed before #527's commit, and asked that they be FILED; the 2026-10-02 disposition (regress/artifacts/idlessaudit_20261002/AGY_FLAGS_DISPOSITION.md, flags #10-#14) then made `ppcrldimimask` their carrier -- 'the carrier owes its recorded work whenever its round runs'.  This row carries them now, so that row could close (GPT-6 Astra, #527's closure check).  The five, specified in OUTSTANDING_BUGS.md under `ppcrldimimask` -- SHIPPED: (1) ADD a full-mask patterned rldimi row at SH=63, MB=1 from 0xDEADBEEFCAFEF00D, want 0xEF56DF77E57F7806 (costs a table 4 and pin 29 -> 30); (2) an alias row at SH=40, MB=40 for a stale rS re-read on WRAPPING masks (codex's arithmetic, not built); (3) an insertion skipped only when Rc=1 survives both probes (both CONTRACTs disclose it); (4) CENSUS_SHRINK -- one run of the fixed build with a shortened census, the literal pins' unique channel; (5) R_NOGUARD -- delete rlwimi's `sh ?` guard, predicted 28/28, load-bearing for definedness since the fix narrowed tmp (Fable)."

 succeeded in 283ms:

POLARITY: **WANT IS POST-FIX CORRECT**, the house convention -- so a kill row wants `alive' and
its PRE-FIX FAIL *IS* the reproduction.  Written want=DEAD first, which scored a tidy 9/9 on the
defect and would have gone RED after a correct fix, reading as though the fix broke something.

*** ORACLE POLARITY -- EOF ALONE IS THE KILL. ***  The text is DIAGNOSIS, not half the trigger.
A build that still abort()s with a REWORDED message gives EOF and no matching text; an
EOF-AND-text oracle would never fire and would certify a live defect GREEN.  That lesson was
bought on the ARM MSR spec this same day and is applied here rather than re-learned.
"""
import os
import pty
import re
import select
import signal
import sys
import time

BIN = sys.argv[1] if len(sys.argv) > 1 else "../../../build/gxemul"
LABEL = sys.argv[2] if len(sys.argv) > 2 else "?"

#  The stub is a GENERATED artefact, never committed (top-level regress/*.bin is NEVER STAGE).
#  All 11 top-level probes that reference such a stub create it if absent; this does the same,
#  so the probe runs on a fresh clone.
DUMMY = os.path.join(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)), "ip30_dummy.bin")
if not os.path.exists(DUMMY):
    with open(DUMMY, "wb") as f:
        f.write(b"\0" * 8)

CODE = 0x80001000
SENTINEL = 0x5a5a5a5a
RAMPLANT = 0x11223344

#  KSEG1 (uncached), sign-extended the way the file's own :113 comment prints it:
#  "Address: 0xffffffffaff10018".  base 0x0ff00000 -> 0xffffffffaff00000.
BASE = 0xFFFFFFFFAFF00000
A_BANKCFG = BASE + 0x00020     # case 0x20    -> 0x80010000, the DEVICE SIGNATURE
A_IMASK0 = BASE + 0x10000      # case 0x10000 -> implemented r/w
A_R10018 = BASE + 0x10018      # case 0x10018 -> implemented r/w
A_SETISR = BASE + 0x10020      # case 0x10020 -> PREDICTED KILL, and no writeflag test
A_CLRISR = BASE + 0x10028      # case 0x10028 -> PREDICTED KILL, and no writeflag test
A_ISR = BASE + 0x10030         # case 0x10030 -> writeflag-TESTED; READ predicted SERVICED
A_C20000 = BASE + 0x20000    # case 0x20000 -> implemented r/w counter
A_C30000 = BASE + 0x30000    # case 0x30000 -> implemented r/w
A_RAM = 0xFFFFFFFF80002000     # KSEG0 RAM, for the liveness control

OP_LW_V0_AT = 0x8C220000       # lw   $v0, 0($at)
OP_SW_T0_A3 = 0xACE80000       # sw   $t0, 0($a3)
#  *** 64-BIT FORMS ARE NOT OPTIONAL FOR imask0.  `case 0x10000' does
#  `d->imask0 = idata' with `idata = memory_readmax64(cpu, data, len)', so a 4-BYTE
#  `sw' CAPS idata BELOW 2^32 AND BIT 50 CAN NEVER BE SET.  Measured: sw 0xffffffff
#  + 70000 steps -> ALIVE.  A tick row built with OP_SW_T0_A3 would arm NOTHING,
#  stay alive, and score GREEN ON A LIVE HOST DEATH. ***
OP_SD_T0_A3 = 0xFCE80000       # sd   $t0, 0($a3)   -- REQUIRED to reach bit 50
OP_LD_V0_AT = 0xDC220000       # ld   $v0, 0($at)   -- its readback
OP_B_SELF = 0x1000FFFF         # b    .
OP_NOP = 0x00000000

rows = []


def row(name, got, want, note=""):
    rows.append((name, str(got), str(want), note))


def session(cmds, settle=2.0, spin=2.5):
    """One fresh process per SESSION -- most sessions score one row, but
    `tick 50`/`tick 50 txt` and `xbit isr`/`xbit tick` each score two rows from
    one process, by design (the cross-bit mutant needs both announce classes in
    one device lifetime) (#561).  Returns (transcript, alive)."""
    pid, fd = pty.fork()
    if pid == 0:
        os.execv(BIN, [BIN, "-V", "-x", "-E", "sgi", "-e", "ip30", "-M", "64",
                       "0x%x:" % CODE + DUMMY])
        os._exit(127)
    buf = ""

    def rd(t):
        nonlocal buf
        end = time.time() + t
        while time.time() < end:
            try:
                r, _, _ = select.select([fd], [], [], 0.1)
            except OSError:
                return
            if not r:
                continue
            try:
                d = os.read(fd, 65536)
            except OSError:
                return
            if not d:
                return
            buf += d.decode("utf-8", "replace")

    rd(settle)
    for c in cmds:
        try:
            os.write(fd, (c + "\n").encode())
        except OSError:
            break
        rd(0.35)
    rd(spin)

    #  *** POLL, NEVER SAMPLE ONCE.  MEASURED 2026-09-17, and the first run of this probe
    #  reported `alive' for a process that SIGABRT'd 0.6 s later. ***
    #  `rd()' RETURNS IMMEDIATELY ON EOF rather than waiting out its timeout, so `spin' --
    #  which exists precisely to give a dying child time to die -- is SKIPPED EXACTLY WHEN THE
    #  CHILD DIES.  A single waitpid(WNOHANG) then lands ~0 s after EOF while the kernel is
    #  still writing a 6 MB core, reports "still running", and THE KILL ROW GOES GREEN ON A
    #  LIVE HOST DEATH.  That is the false-green this probe exists to refuse.
    alive = True
    deadline = time.time() + 12.0
    while time.time() < deadline:
        try:
            wpid, status = os.waitpid(pid, os.WNOHANG)
        except ChildProcessError:
            alive = False
            break
        if wpid == pid:
            alive = False
            break
        time.sleep(0.05)
    if alive:
        try:
            os.kill(pid, signal.SIGKILL)
            os.waitpid(pid, 0)
        except OSError:
            pass
    try:
        os.close(fd)
    except OSError:
        pass
    return buf, alive


def run_ops(ops, at=CODE):
    put = ["put w 0x%x, 0x%08x" % (at + 4 * i, op) for i, op in enumerate(ops)]
    put += ["put w 0x%x, 0x%08x" % (at + 4 * len(ops), OP_B_SELF),
            "put w 0x%x, 0x%08x" % (at + 4 * len(ops) + 4, OP_NOP)]
    return put + ["pc=0x%x" % at, "step %d" % len(ops)]


def guest_load(addr):
    """A REAL guest instruction through real decode and real memory_rw -- rung 3.
    NOT `dump': all four ip30 registrations are DM_DEFAULT, so dump BYPASSES the handler
    and would prove nothing about the device at all."""
    return ["at=0x%x" % addr, "v0=0x%x" % SENTINEL] + run_ops([OP_LW_V0_AT]) + ["print v0"]


def guest_store(addr, val):
    return ["a3=0x%x" % addr, "t0=0x%x" % val] + run_ops([OP_SW_T0_A3])


def guest_store64(addr, val):
    """A 64-BIT store.  The ONLY way to reach imask0 bit 50 -- see OP_SD_T0_A3."""
    return ["a3=0x%x" % addr, "t0=0x%x" % val] + run_ops([OP_SD_T0_A3])


def guest_load64(addr):
    return ["at=0x%x" % addr, "v0=0x%x" % SENTINEL] + run_ops([OP_LD_V0_AT]) + ["print v0"]


def printed_last(t, reg):
    """*** THE LAST `print <reg>', NOT THE FIRST. ***  L1 repair 2026-09-17.

    `printed()' uses `re.search', which returns the FIRST match.  A row that issues
    MORE THAN ONE guest_load therefore reads the WRONG load's value, silently -- and
    `isr keep' does three commands ending in the read-back it actually wants.

    PRE-FIX THE BUG WAS INVISIBLE because the row's seeding write aborted and the row
    read `died'; the construction defect only surfaced once the fix let the session
    survive.  A row that cannot pass even on a correct fix is vacuous, so this is L1
    construction, repaired in-round rather than filed."""
    m = re.findall(r"print\s+%s\s*\n\s*(0x[0-9a-f]+)" % reg, t)
    return m[-1] if m else "ABSENT"


def counted(t, needle):
    """*** HOW MANY TIMES DID THIS ANNOUNCE FIRE? ***  Added by the #531 class closure.

    Presence is not enough for the LATCH cells.  A defeated latch (mask -> 0) announces on
    EVERY access and a presence oracle reads `yes' either way -- the CHANNEL vacuity, one
    level along.  Only a COUNT varies under that mutant."""
    return t.count(needle)


def printed(t, reg):
    """`print <reg>' emits a BARE 0x... -- `reg' is the command that carries the `r0 = ' prefix.
    Copied from regress/lca_isalane_probe.py rather than invented."""
    m = re.search(r"print\s+%s\s*\n\s*(0x[0-9a-f]+)" % reg, t)
    return m.group(1) if m else "ABSENT"


# ------------------------------------------------------------------ CONTROL=DEAD set
#  If any of these reds the vehicle is not the vehicle, and NO kill row may be scored.
t, alive = session(["put w 0x%x, 0x%08x" % (A_RAM & 0xFFFFFFFF, RAMPLANT)]
                   + guest_load(A_RAM))
live_got = printed(t, "v0") if alive else "died"
row("live", live_got, "0x%x" % RAMPLANT,
#!/bin/bash
# Shared helpers for the regression gates.
#
# Two rules encoded here, both learned by getting them wrong:
#
#  1. RUN UNBUFFERED. When gxemul's stdout is a pipe, libc switches to 4 KB block
#     buffering. `timeout` then kills it with SIGTERM and the partial block is lost, so a
#     guest that produced 3 KB of perfectly good boot output scores ZERO bytes while one
#     that produced 5 KB scores 4096. An early version of this harness compared those
#     numbers across builds and "found" a capability regression that was pure buffering.
#     Every emulator invocation goes through run_emu() or run_emu_progress(), both of which
#     force stdbuf -o0 -e0.  (#419 note: run_emu() itself now has NO CALLERS -- gate 7 was
#     its last one.  It is kept because the rule is general and a future gate will want the
#     simple form, but do not cite it as the universal path: run_emu_progress() is.)
#
#  2. A MISSING INPUT IS A HARD ERROR, NEVER A ZERO SCORE. The same early version had no
#     existence check on the baseline binaries, so a wrong path looked exactly like a
#     total behavioural failure. need_file() aborts the gate instead.
#
# Verdicts are PASS / FAIL / SKIP. A SKIP is never counted as a PASS.

ROOT=${ROOT:-/mnt/c/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL}
IMAGES=$ROOT/_images
LOGDIR=${LOGDIR:-/tmp/gxregress}
#  d1: EXPORT, or the driver cannot see it.  A plain assignment here reaches the gates'
#  own shell redirections but NOT a python child, so drive_guest.py kept writing its two
#  pty logs to the hardcoded default while every other artefact relocated -- a mutation
#  census then poisoned the shared logs gate 6 grades.  Measured: without this line a
#  caller who writes `LOGDIR=x ./run.sh` propagates (env-prefixed vars are exported) but a
#  caller who writes `LOGDIR=x; ./run.sh` does not, so the defect was CONDITIONALLY silent.
export LOGDIR
mkdir -p "$LOGDIR"

#  #426: classify a rig's reported budget.  IT LIVES HERE, NOT IN THE GATE, so the branch
#  logic can be exercised offline by a selftest instead of only under a weekly rig boot.
#  Echoes ONE DISTINGUISHABLE TOKEN per case:
#    absent      the rig deliberately has no budget (landisk: its count nearly halves under
#                host load, so any ceiling would be invented rather than measured)
#    calibrated  a value inside the range measured for that rig
#    zeroed      ZERO ON A RIG THAT IS CALIBRATED -- the case that used to print a green
#                "deliberately absent".  MEASURED: a luna88k run reporting BUDGET=0 passed
#                11/11 while the row said something false about a 12 G rig, and the driver's
#                own ceiling went falsy at the same time.  RED, not a skip: the gate HOLDS the
#                calibration, so a skip would claim an ignorance it does not have.
#    out-of-range / unreported  as they say.
budget_class() {
    #  ${2-} because every gate here runs under `set -u`, where a one-argument call would
    #  abort the gate with "$2: unbound variable" instead of classifying.  A classifier that
    #  kills its caller on a malformed call is worse than one that says `unreported`.
    case "${1-}:${2-}" in
    landisk:0)   echo absent ;;
    luna88k:0)   echo zeroed ;;
    *:)          echo unreported ;;
    luna88k:*)   if [ "$2" -ge 8174849291 ] 2>/dev/null && [ "$2" -le 15571141508 ]
                 then echo calibrated; else echo out-of-range; fi ;;
    *:0)         echo absent ;;
    *)           echo uncalibrated-rig ;;
    esac
}

C_OK=$'\033[32m'; C_BAD=$'\033[31m'; C_SKIP=$'\033[33m'; C_OFF=$'\033[0m'
[ -t 1 ] || { C_OK=""; C_BAD=""; C_SKIP=""; C_OFF=""; }

# Exit codes. SKIP is 77, NOT 2, because bash exits 2 on a SYNTAX ERROR -- so with 2 as
# the skip code a typo in any gate was silently downgraded to "coverage gap" and run.sh
# still exited 0. Anything non-zero that is not 77 is a failure.
EXIT_SKIP=77

GATE_NAME=""
_fails=0
_checks=0

gate_begin() { GATE_NAME=$1; _fails=0; _checks=0
    echo "############################################################"
    echo "## GATE: $GATE_NAME"
    echo "############################################################"
}

# check <description> <actual> <expected>
check() {
    _checks=$((_checks+1))
    if [ "$2" = "$3" ]; then
        printf "  ${C_OK}ok${C_OFF}   %-52s %s\n" "$1" "$2"
    else
        printf "  ${C_BAD}FAIL${C_OFF} %-52s got=%s want=%s\n" "$1" "$2" "$3"
        _fails=$((_fails+1))
    fi
}

# check_min <description> <actual> <minimum>
check_min() {
    _checks=$((_checks+1))
    if [ "$2" -ge "$3" ] 2>/dev/null; then
        printf "  ${C_OK}ok${C_OFF}   %-52s %s (>= %s)\n" "$1" "$2" "$3"
    else
        printf "  ${C_BAD}FAIL${C_OFF} %-52s got=%s want>=%s\n" "$1" "$2" "$3"
        _fails=$((_fails+1))
    fi
}

note() { printf "  --   %s\n" "$*"; }

# A gate may declare that part of its coverage did not run (a rig whose image is absent,
# say). That must not be absorbed into a PASS: it downgrades the whole gate to SKIP, so a
# missing input can never be reported as evidence of correctness.
_degraded=0
degrade() { _degraded=1; printf "  ${C_SKIP}skip${C_OFF} %s\n" "$*"; }

gate_end() {
    echo
    if [ "$_checks" = 0 ]; then
        echo "${C_SKIP}$GATE_NAME: SKIP${C_OFF} (no checks ran)"; return $EXIT_SKIP
    elif [ "$_fails" != 0 ]; then
        echo "${C_BAD}$GATE_NAME: FAIL${C_OFF} ($_fails of $_checks checks)"; return 1
    elif [ "$_degraded" != 0 ]; then
        echo "${C_SKIP}$GATE_NAME: SKIP${C_OFF} ($_checks checks passed, but part of the gate could not run)"
        return $EXIT_SKIP
    else
        echo "${C_OK}$GATE_NAME: PASS${C_OFF} ($_checks checks)"; return 0
    fi
}

#  #371: gate_skip() exits with the SKIP code, which run.sh maps to
#  REGRESS_PASS_WITH_GAPS -- a green-ish verdict. It never consulted the running
#  failure counter, so a gate that had ALREADY recorded red checks and then hit a
#  gate_skip (a probe that produced no result line, a missing rig image) reported
#  those reds as a skip and they vanished from the battery. Measured on a
#  synthetic gate: one FAIL then gate_skip exited 77, PASS_WITH_GAPS. This is the
#  same "a green row means nothing" class the gate rows themselves guard against,
#  in the harness's own control flow.
#
#  So a gate_skip AFTER failures is a FAIL, not a skip: the skip cannot un-record
#  what already failed. A gate_skip with a clean slate stays a genuine skip (a
#  preflight that could not run at all -- need_file/need_exec). degrade() was
#  already correct: gate_end() tests _fails before _degraded, so a degraded gate
#!/bin/bash
# GATE 14 -- ARM subtract-family carry flags (#311) and undefined routing (#312).
#
# What this protects
# -----------------
# #311: the subtract family computed its carry-out as `a >= b`. That is
# NOT-BORROW for SUB/CMP/RSB, which have no borrow-in, and WRONG for SBC/RSC,
# whose result is `a - b - NOT(C)`. The two disagree exactly when `a == b` with
# carry-in clear: `a - a - 1` borrows, so carry must be CLEAR, and `a >= b`
# reported it SET. The fix takes the flag from the full 64-bit result the file
# already computes (`c32 == c64`), which is the same answer as `a >= b` for the
# three instructions that were already right.
#
# #312: ARM's permanently-undefined encodings reached `goto bad`, which sets
# cpu->running = 0 (cpu_dyntrans.c) -- a legal-to-attempt instruction stopping
# the whole emulator, the same halt class as #264/#309/#310. They now raise the
# Undefined Instruction exception the silicon raises.
#
# This gate is known to be able to FAIL
# ------------------------------------
# It was run against the committed pre-fix build and scored 39 of the 56 rows it
# had at that moment, failing in exactly the 17 places the three fixes were
# predicted to flip and nowhere else. The two `subs rn=pc` pins were added after
# that sweep and pass either way, so the same build on today's table would read
# 41/58 -- stated exactly rather than restated as 39/58, because the count is
# evidence and evidence does not get rounded to the number that sounds better.
# That measurement is what shows these rows discriminate; gate 3's mutant
# machinery does not reach here, because it operates on float_emul.c and this
# gate measures the real emulator instead of a pure function.
#
# Swept again for #346 against a binary built from the parent commit: 162 of
# 165, failing the three cache-clean rows the fix flips and nowhere else. The
# two cache-clean CONTROL rows pass on both builds, which is what they are for.
#
# And again for #347 against a binary built from ITS parent (be6ea08): 168 of
# 173, failing exactly the five `A cclean2 ... ` discriminators and nowhere
# else. All three of that round's control/anti-clobber pins pass on both builds.
#
# And for round 99 (#348/#349/#350) against a binary built from the pre-fix
# HEAD (dea2fef): 181 of 190, failing exactly the NINE new DISC rows -- the
# two flags rows, the tail/zero/tail-V flag rows, the two fires rows,
# `A cacheclean nonmult` reading "fold", and `A cacheclean zero n` reading
# "none" -- and nowhere else. On the fixed build: 190/190. The retired
# `A cclean2 still fold` control asserted the MISSING flags and was replaced
# in the same change by the #349 marker rows, exactly as its own comment
# required. The nonmult witness's first draft is itself a recorded lesson:
# it expected a data abort at the top of RAM (measured false -- non-existent
# reads log and continue) and compared a dump string unswapped, so it read
# its own sentinel's parity; see run_cc_nonmult's docstring. Its "live"
# verdict was then tightened in review to also demand load progress (r0
# moved off 0x9120), closing a false pass against a guard that returns
# without calling the load.
#
# Why most of this gate is PINs
# ----------------------------

 exited 1 in 320ms:
    #  a test deterministic removed the last coverage of the value it replaces.*
    #
    #  This row runs on the REAL clock, with one exemption dated YESTERDAY -- computed,
    #  never a literal, or the row rots into a permanent red the day it is written.
    #  Clean checker: rc=1, EXPIRED EXEMPTION.  Frozen clock: rc=0, PROBEWIRING_PASS.
    if EX is None:
        results.append(False)
        print("  FAIL  M5f -- no exempt DETECTOR (see above).")
    else:
        import datetime as _dt
        _yest = (_dt.date.today() - _dt.timedelta(days=1)).isoformat()
        rg, chk = fresh()
        _st_apply(chk, _exline(EX), '    "%s":   ("%s", "x"),%s' % (EX, _yest, chr(10)))
        case("M5f the DEFAULT clock is live (no --today)", 1,
             "EXPIRED EXEMPTION  %s" % EX, chk, rg)

    rg, chk = fresh()
    with open(os.path.join(rg, "zz_new_probe.py"), "w", encoding="utf-8",
              newline="\n") as fh:
        fh.write("#!/usr/bin/env python3\n")
    case("M6  a NEW probe arriving unclassified reddens", 1,
         "UNCLASSIFIED  zz_new_probe.py", chk, rg)

    rg, chk = fresh(); os.remove(os.path.join(rg, "pit8253_latch_probe.py"))
    case("M7  a MANIFEST entry whose file is gone reddens", 1,
         "GHOST  the MANIFEST names pit8253_latch_probe.py", chk, rg)

    rg, chk = fresh()
    _st_apply(chk, _lit('"pit8253_latch_probe.py"', ':      (CLASS_DETECTOR'),
              _lit('"pit8253_latch_probe.py"', ':      (CLASS_TOOL'))
    case("M8  hiding a detector in class 'tool' reddens", 1,
         "MISFILED  pit8253_latch_probe.py", chk, rg)

    rg, chk = fresh()
    _st_apply(os.path.join(rg, "run.sh"), " gate_arm gate_ppc_halt", " gate_ppc_halt")
    case("M9  dropping gate_arm from GATES unwires its detectors", 1,  # (#560)
         "UNWIRED DETECTOR  arm_flags_probe.py", chk, rg)

    rg, chk = fresh(); os.remove(os.path.join(rg, "gate_ppc.sh"))
    case("M10 a gate named in GATES with no file reddens", 1,
         "run.sh names gate_ppc.sh", chk, rg)

    rg, chk = fresh(); _st_apply(os.path.join(rg, "run.sh"), "GATES=(", "GATESX=(")
    case("M11 an unparseable GATES array reddens", 1, "no GATES=( ... ) array", chk, rg)

    rg, chk = fresh()
    #  GUARDED, because a missing exemplar is ALREADY recorded as four failures above
    #  and a traceback here would bury that legible report under a stack trace.  The
    #  denominator is held the same way: one False, not one fewer case.
    if EX is None:
        results.append(False)
        print("  FAIL  M12 -- no exempt DETECTOR could be extracted (see above).")
    else:
        #  DERIVED.  This named `hpcmips_ctor_probe.py` literally and was the THIRD
        #  such literal in this selftest -- found by a seat AFTER two earlier repairs
        #  had each believed they were the last.  The tripwire was moved twice before
        #  it was removed, which is the argument for deriving rather than renaming.
        _st_apply(chk, _exline(EX),
                  _exline(EX).replace('"%s"' % EX, '"hpcabort_witness.py"', 1))
        case("M12 exempting a WITNESS reddens", 1,
             "ORPHAN EXEMPTION  hpcabort_witness.py", chk, rg)

    #  ---------------------------------------------------------------- #471
    #  THE RECURSIVE SCAN NEEDS ITS OWN MUTANTS, or a future edit reverts it and every
    #  mutant above stays green -- the vacuity this file exists to refuse.  The three
    #  below were specified by the farmed design that scoped this fix.

    #  M13: NESTED RED.  Delete the real invocation from the gate; the nested detector
    #  must be named by its FULL RELATIVE PATH, not its basename.
    rg, chk = fresh()
    _st_apply(os.path.join(rg, "gate_sh_rounding.sh"),
              'python3 -u "$GPNPROBE"', 'true "$GPNPROBE"')
    case("M13 a NESTED detector loses its gate and reddens", 1,
         "artifacts/gdrompionull/gdrom_pio_null_probe.py", chk, rg)

    #  M14: THE SCAN ITSELF.  Restore the `"/" not in f` filter and the nested detector
    #  becomes INVISIBLE -- which is exactly the #465 escape.  It reddens as a GHOST,
    #  because the MANIFEST still names a file the scan can no longer see.
    rg, chk = fresh()
    _st_apply(chk, _lit('rel = os.path.relpath(', 'os.path.join(dirpath, f), regress)'),
                   _lit('rel = ', 'f'))
    case("M14 the walk flattened (the #465 blind spot returns)", 1,
         "GHOST", chk, rg)

    #  M15: THE COLLISION CONTROL.  Re-key exec sites to the bare name again.  A gate
    #  invoking
    #  one nested detector would then mark EVERY like-named file gated -- the silent
    #  failure the path re-key exists to prevent.  (This comment deliberately avoids
    #  quoting the mutant's own find-text: _st_apply saw it TWICE and refused the
    #  edit, which is the harness correctly rejecting an ambiguous mutant.)
    #  It reddens because the ignored
    #  branch swallows the nested invocation instead.
    #  [#556, 2026-10-02 -- a records correction; the text above is kept as it was written] It reddens because the
    #  nested probe is keyed under its bare basename rather than its manifest relative path.
    #  (hcheckprobewiring:F18: regress/artifacts/astraretro_harness_20260926/HARNESS_DISPOSITIONS.md)
    rg, chk = fresh()
    _st_apply(chk, _lit('hits.setdefault(', 'rel, []).append'),
                   _lit('hits.setdefault(', 'b, []).append'))
    case("M15 exec sites keyed by basename again (collision)", 1,
         "artifacts/gdrompionull/gdrom_pio_null_probe.py", chk, rg)

    shutil.rmtree(root, ignore_errors=True)
    n_ok = sum(1 for r in results if r)
    print()
    if n_ok != len(results):
        print("PROBEWIRING_SELFTEST_FAIL  %d/%d mutants behaved as specified"
              % (n_ok, len(results)))
        return 1
    print("PROBEWIRING_SELFTEST_PASS  %d/%d mutants behaved as specified"
          % (n_ok, len(results)))
    return 0


def main(argv):
    verbose = "-v" in argv or "--verbose" in argv
    if "--selftest" in argv:
        return selftest(verbose)
    regress = DEFAULT_REGRESS
    today = None
    for i, a in enumerate(argv):
        if a == "--regress" and i + 1 < len(argv):
            regress = os.path.abspath(argv[i + 1])
        if a == "--today" and i + 1 < len(argv):
            today = argv[i + 1]
    if today is None:
        import datetime
        today = datetime.date.today().isoformat()

    fails, notes = [], []

    if not os.path.isdir(regress):
        print("PROBEWIRING_FAIL  no regress dir at %s" % regress)
        return 1

    scripts, err = gate_list(regress)
    if err:
        print("  FAIL  %s" % err)
        print("PROBEWIRING_FAIL  the battery could not be derived")
        return 1
    scripts = scripts + [s for s in ALWAYS if s not in scripts]

    hits, ignored, missing = exec_sites(regress, scripts)
    for s in missing:
        fails.append("run.sh names %s and the file does not exist -- the battery is broken" % s)

    on_disk, mode = domain(regress)

    for f in on_disk:
        if f not in MANIFEST:
            fails.append("UNCLASSIFIED  %s is not in check_probe_wiring.py's MANIFEST.\n"
                         "                classify it detector (green once fixed), witness "
                         "(red once fixed) or tool." % f)
    for f in sorted(MANIFEST):
        if f not in on_disk:
            #  *** THE MESSAGE USED TO SAY "regress/ has no such file".  THAT IS A WRONG
            #  RECORD, and it discredits a TRUE finding: domain() is `git ls-files' --
            #  COMMITTED-OR-STAGED, as its own docstring says in capitals -- so an UNTRACKED
            #  probe is reported here while sitting plainly in regress/.  A reader who
            #  followed the old wording found the file, concluded this check was broken, and
            #  dismissed a real one.  Say what is actually true. ***
            fails.append("GHOST  the MANIFEST names %s and it is NOT COMMITTED OR STAGED "
                         "(domain() reads `git ls-files', not the directory) -- `git add' it "
                         "if it is real, or delete the MANIFEST entry" % f)

    rows = []
    for f in on_disk:
        if f not in MANIFEST:
            continue
        cls, why = MANIFEST[f]
        where = hits.get(f, [])
        if cls not in CLASSES:
            fails.append("BAD CLASS  %s is classified '%s'; want one of %s"
                         % (f, cls, "/".join(CLASSES)))
            continue

        if cls == CLASS_TOOL and (f.endswith("_probe.py") or f.endswith("_witness.py")):
            fails.append("MISFILED  %s is classified 'tool'. A file named *_probe.py or "
                         "*_witness.py asserts something; classify it detector or witness."
                         % f)

        if cls == CLASS_DETECTOR:
            if where:
                state = "RUN by " + ", ".join(where)
                if f in EXEMPT:
                    fails.append("STALE EXEMPTION  %s is RUN by %s and still carries an "
                                 "exemption dated %s -- the debt is paid, delete the line"
                                 % (f, where[0], EXEMPT[f][0]))
            elif f in EXEMPT:
                d = EXEMPT[f][0]
                if not DATE_RE.match(d or ""):
                    fails.append("MALFORMED EXEMPTION  %s:'%s' is not YYYY-MM-DD. A date "
                                 "nothing validates never expires -- refusing to guess."
                                 % (f, d))
                    state = "EXEMPT(BAD-DATE)"
                elif d < today:
                    fails.append("EXPIRED EXEMPTION  %s came due %s (today %s) and is still "
                                 "run by no gate" % (f, d, today))
                    state = "EXEMPT(EXPIRED %s)" % d
                else:
                    state = "EXEMPT until %s" % d
            else:
                fails.append("UNWIRED DETECTOR  %s is run by NO gate and has no dated "
                             "exemption.\n                wire it into a gate, or add a dated "
                             "line to EXEMPT naming the gate that owes it." % f)
                state = "UNWIRED"
        elif cls == CLASS_WITNESS:
            if where:
                fails.append("GATED WITNESS  %s is invoked at %s. A witness asserts the "
                             "PRE-FIX symptom, so it goes RED the day the fix lands -- "
                             "gating it manufactures a regression." % (f, where[0]))
                state = "GATED (must not be): " + ", ".join(where)
            else:
                state = "not run (correct)"
        else:
            state = ("RUN by " + ", ".join(where)) if where else "-"

        if cls in (CLASS_DETECTOR, CLASS_WITNESS):
            lbl = self_label(os.path.join(regress, f))
            if lbl and lbl != cls:
                notes.append("SELFLABEL  %s: manifest says %s, its own summary line says %s. "
                             "Advisory only -- self-labels are measurably unreliable in both "
                             "directions." % (f, cls, lbl))
        rows.append((cls, f, state, why))

    for f in sorted(EXEMPT):
        if f not in MANIFEST:
            fails.append("ORPHAN EXEMPTION  %s is exempted and is not in the MANIFEST" % f)
        elif MANIFEST[f][0] != CLASS_DETECTOR:
            fails.append("ORPHAN EXEMPTION  %s is classified '%s'; only a detector can be "
                         "exempted from being run" % (f, MANIFEST[f][0]))

    print("  check_probe_wiring: %d python artefacts in %s/ [%s], %d battery scripts "
          "from run.sh" % (len(on_disk), os.path.basename(regress), mode, len(scripts)))
    if verbose:
        for cls in CLASSES:
            for c, f, state, why in rows:
                if c == cls:
                    print("    %-8s %-28s %-38s %s" % (c, f, state, why))
        for line in ignored:
            print("    IGNORED  %s   (not the regress copy)" % line)
    for n in notes:
        print("  note  %s" % n)
    for f in fails:
        print("  FAIL  %s" % f)

    det = [r for r in rows if r[0] == CLASS_DETECTOR]
    run = [r for r in det if r[2].startswith("RUN")]
    ex = [r for r in det if r[2].startswith("EXEMPT")]
    wit = [r for r in rows if r[0] == CLASS_WITNESS]
    if fails:
        print("PROBEWIRING_FAIL  %d problem(s); %d/%d detectors run by a gate, %d dated-exempt"
              % (len(fails), len(run), len(det), len(ex)))
        return 1
    print("PROBEWIRING_PASS  %d/%d detectors run by a gate, %d dated-exempt, %d witnesses "
          "correctly ungated" % (len(run), len(det), len(ex), len(wit)))
    return 0


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main(sys.argv[1:]))

