VERDICT: 4 flags -- scoring logic is sound; correct the load disclosure and three stale records before closure.

Q1. The row patterns handle the actual protocol correctly. `%-12s` specifies a minimum width, so longer names and values retain the required separator. All current got/want sources produce whitespace-free tokens. Prefix pairs cannot collide because the shorter name must be followed by spaces and `got=`.

The denominator patterns cover every current CONTROL=OK row, including FAIL rows. DEAD’s statusless rows escape both intentionally; CONTROL, the named checks, and the zero denominator reject that run. A malformed replacement row also loses its required named match. Arbitrary extra malformed text can be ignored: “rows emitted” counts recognized status-bearing rows, not every possible log line.

Q2. Parse-before-score is sufficient for this producer. Missing, malformed, or duplicate RESULT/CONTROL records and missing/duplicate exact DONE records fail parsing. DEAD fails scoring even though its report parses and its exit status is zero.

The exit-status check adds real protection: a probe can print a complete good report and then terminate abnormally. The synchronous invocation waits for termination, and `ip30rc` rejects that case. Ordinary interleaved noise is harmless; the checks do not enforce ordering or require DONE to be the final line.

Q3. Keep the existing artifacts path. It preserves the witness references and frozen-record relationships, and the GD-ROM gate confirms this placement is supported. A copy creates avoidable divergence. Section U’s docstring omission is real: I reproduced `35` pinned sets with only `13` docstrings checked.

FLAG: The newly cited [probe-header contract](C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/artifacts/ip30abortkill/ip30_abort_probe.py:20) is stale: it describes six announce sites, read-side `latch 1x`, fourteen cells with six covered, and closure still owed. The final implementation describes four announce sites, ten cells, write-side latch tests, and completed closure. Qualify the historical contract and state the current one in place; moving the file is unnecessary.

Q4. The approximately 568-second cost and wall-clock dependence are accurate. Neither `run.sh` nor `nightly_battery.sh` imposes an overall timeout. `nightly_check.sh`’s default 176-hour threshold measures verdict freshness, not execution duration.

The installed [weekly task XML](C:/Windows/System32/Tasks/GXemul-weekly-battery) omits `ExecutionTimeLimit`, leaving Windows’ documented default of 72 hours. The previous battery took approximately four hours; another 9.5 minutes does not approach that limit. This is an estimate, not a measurement of the revised battery. [Microsoft documentation](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/taskschd/tasksettings-executiontimelimit)

FLAG: Make the [load disclosure](C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/gate_arm.sh:1519) explicitly include false greens. On poll expiry, `session()` kills the child but returns `alive=True`. A stalled `kill 20 rd` or `kill 28 rd` session can therefore pass both survival and expected-silence checks before executing its access. Earlier controls ran in separate sessions. This requires an honest limitation statement, not a timing redesign within this wiring round.

Q5. The four legs are appropriate. I verified that #531 changed only `dev_sgi_ip30.c` under `src/`, and its parent’s file has the same Git blob as the upstream import. Restoring that file reinstates all four abort sites. Preserve each trigger’s failing rows; one aggregate red alone does not establish observation of every site.

A device-absent build is not additionally owed. The [2026-10-09 ruling](C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/artifacts/fablequeue7n_20261009/fable5_rule7n_12.md:35) accepts absent/non-emulator binaries for runtime probes and rejects “a sharper medium exists” as a floor criterion.

Distinguish the absent-binary **block** result from the complete gate: `need_exec "$PMAX"` skips the latter before reaching this block. `/bin/true` satisfies that prerequisite.

Before landing, retain the promised completed legs and full gate run, and extend the scoring controls with:

- A complete green report with nonzero `ip30rc`, exercising death after DONE.
- Malformed/duplicate CONTROL and duplicate DONE.
- A missing probe invocation.
